# Amendment cycle — namespaced-labels-and-bootout (#6, 2026-04-22,
# sixth amendment): amendment #5 landed a clean detached first-run
# but a real-world fresh-clone install (Luke's pos3 workspace) still
# halted at phase-4b-health-poll with `service-health-timeout:com.
# pos.orchestrator`. Root cause: ServiceManagerRunner.bootstrap called
# `launchctl bootstrap gui/<uid> <plist>` without first issuing a
# `launchctl bootout gui/<uid>/<label>` — launchd treats bootstrap as
# a no-op when the label is already loaded, so any cached path from a
# prior install (the test-harness tempdir in Luke's case) survives
# across the scaffold's plist rewrite. Additional defect: service
# labels were hard-coded (`com.pos.orchestrator`, `com.pos-v2.memory-
# graphiti`), so two pos-v2 clones on one host would collide on a
# single launchd/systemd-user identity.
#
# Amendment #6 closes both:
#   - Derives a per-workspace slug from the workspace-root basename
#     (lowercased, sanitised to `[a-z0-9-]+`, leading/trailing '-'
#     trimmed); structural refusal (WorkspaceSlugUnrepresentableError,
#     -32099) when the basename has no valid slug form — no unnamespaced
#     service file is ever written.
#   - Templates launchd plist / systemd unit labels as
#     `com.pos-v2.<slug>.<kind>`; filenames match label. Two workspaces
#     on one host coexist because their labels differ.
#   - Bootout-before-bootstrap in ServiceManagerRunner.bootstrap: on
#     macOS, launchctl bootout first (non-fatal on "service not loaded"
#     stderr variants; structural refusal via ServiceManagerBootoutError
#     on any other failure) then bootstrap. On Linux, stop +
#     daemon-reload before start — symmetric semantic. Idempotent on
#     re-run.
#   - Inventory (first-run-inventory.yaml) templates service labels
#     with `{slug}`; resolve_service_labels() in first_run_inventory.py
#     substitutes at helper load-time so Phase 4b health poll targets
#     the computed labels.
#
# Multi-component amendment (hands-off-lifecycle + workspace-bootstrap).
# Nine acceptance criteria AC1–AC9 in docs/rebuild/components/
