# Amendment cycle — orchestrator-bootstrap-unification (#7,
# 2026-04-22, seventh amendment): pos-v2 had two unrelated systems
# both called "bootstrap" that were never reconciled. The
# orchestrator's native loader (orchestrator/src/bootstrap.py,
# called from Orchestrator._startup) hard-required ~/.pos/bootstrap.py
# — fail-closed with exit code 2 on missing, exit 3 on import error.
# The workspace-bootstrap framework, built later, ships a
# WorkspaceBootstrapPyContribution adapter that loads the same file
# with required=False by default (missing = silent no-op). The
# native loader ran first at startup and fail-closed before the
# adapter ever got a turn. First-run scaffolds bootstrap.yaml
# (framework config), never a bootstrap.py — so every fresh install
# hit the orchestrator's fail-closed exit-2 before the framework
# could compose anything. The pos3 workspace first-run this session
# surfaced it live; blocker 2 in the session's troubleshooting
# series.
#
# Amendment #7 makes the framework canonical:
#   - Orchestrator._startup removes the load_and_register call + the
#     unreachable BootstrapMissing/BootstrapError handlers + the
#     import from .bootstrap. The native bootstrap.py primitive
#     remains as a public surface (still called by the framework's
#     adapter) but zero callers live inside the orchestrator itself.
#   - OrchestratorConfig.require_bootstrap field removed (it existed
#     solely to control the now-dead branch); PrimaryPersonaContribution
#     and two test YAML literals updated in lockstep.
#   - python -m pos_orchestrator --no-bootstrap flag removed
#     (argparse now rejects it; --help omits it). Dev/test semantics
#     were redundant once required=False became the default story.
#   - test_missing_bootstrap_fails_closed, test_erroring_bootstrap_fails_closed,
#     and test_bootstrap_refused_emits_distinct_event deleted — they
#     pinned the exact contract this amendment removes. Doc comments
#     at the deletion sites cite the proposal for audit-trail
#     continuity. AC2 is the positive-space inverse (asserts missing
#     bootstrap.py is no longer fail-closed).
#   - Missing ~/.pos/bootstrap.yaml is the new fail-closed trigger,
#     surfaced by the framework's existing MissingConfigError
#     (-32080) when load_manifest is called on a non-existent path.
#     No new top-level error code introduced.
#   - New orchestrator/tests/test_no_sealed_amendments.py — first
